<svg viewBox="0 0 720 470" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="How a model samples the next token">
  <defs>
    <marker id="ch02sa-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="var(--ink-faint)" />
    </marker>
  </defs>

  <!-- step 1: logits -->
  <rect x="40" y="20" width="640" height="64" rx="10" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="64" y="46" font-size="14" font-weight="550" fill="var(--ink)">1 · Model outputs a logit vector</text>
  <text x="64" y="68" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">one raw score per vocabulary token — can be negative, don’t sum to 1</text>

  <line x1="360" y1="84" x2="360" y2="108" stroke="var(--ink-faint)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ch02sa-arrow)" />
  <text x="376" y="103" font-size="11.5" font-style="italic" fill="var(--accent)">divide logits by temperature</text>

  <!-- step 2: temperature -->
  <rect x="40" y="114" width="640" height="64" rx="10" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="64" y="140" font-size="14" font-weight="550" fill="var(--ink)">2 · Temperature reshapes the distribution</text>
  <text x="64" y="162" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">low T → sharper, safer picks · high T → flatter, rarer tokens surface · T=0 → just take the argmax</text>

  <line x1="360" y1="178" x2="360" y2="202" stroke="var(--ink-faint)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ch02sa-arrow)" />
  <text x="376" y="197" font-size="11.5" font-style="italic" fill="var(--accent)">softmax → probabilities</text>

  <!-- step 3: filter -->
  <rect x="40" y="208" width="640" height="96" rx="10" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="64" y="234" font-size="14" font-weight="550" fill="var(--ink)">3 · Restrict the candidate pool</text>
  <text x="64" y="256" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">top-k: keep only the k highest-scoring tokens (cheaper softmax)</text>
  <text x="64" y="274" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">top-p (nucleus): keep the smallest set whose probabilities sum to p — pool size adapts to context</text>
  <text x="64" y="292" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">constrained sampling: keep only tokens valid under a format grammar (e.g. JSON)</text>

  <line x1="360" y1="304" x2="360" y2="328" stroke="var(--ink-faint)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ch02sa-arrow)" />

  <!-- step 4: sample -->
  <rect x="40" y="334" width="640" height="60" rx="10" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" />
  <text x="64" y="360" font-size="14" font-weight="550" fill="var(--accent-ink)">4 · Sample one token from what remains</text>
  <text x="64" y="380" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">append it to the sequence, then repeat — until a stop token, stop word, or max length</text>

  <line x1="360" y1="394" x2="360" y2="418" stroke="var(--ink-faint)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ch02sa-arrow)" />
  <text x="360" y="440" font-size="12.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">this loop is why every output is a fresh roll of the dice —</text>
  <text x="360" y="458" font-size="12.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">the source of both creativity and inconsistency</text>
</svg>
